fuzz.log of lane t-slice1 (2026-09-30). These runs are SMOKE TESTS, not the long differential run of docs/workflow.md 5.

1. tests/fuzz/fuzz_text_idele.c, built with `make fuzz-build FUZZ_TARGET=text_idele` (clang 18.1.3, libFuzzer, address
   and undefined-behaviour sanitizers), seeded with build/fuzz/corpus/text_idele/ (547 seeds written by
   lanes/t-slice1/seed_corpus.py: the golden rows of the three kinds and 1 in 7 of the generated texts):

       timeout 200 build/fuzz/text_idele build/fuzz/corpus/text_idele -max_total_time=120 -rss_limit_mb=2048

   Result: "Done 3908379 runs in 121 second(s)", 32300 executions per second, 2888 new units added to the corpus,
   peak RSS 463 MB, exit status 0, no crash, no sanitizer report.

   The brief asked for `ulimit -v 4000000`. The sanitized target cannot run under it: AddressSanitizer reserves its
   shadow memory (15392894357504 bytes) and stops with "ReserveShadowMemoryRange failed ... Perhaps you're using ulimit
   -v" (tried, 10 s run). The libFuzzer limit -rss_limit_mb=2048 was used instead.

2. tests/fuzz/fuzz_driver.c (the existing target, unchanged), built again with the new tools/adf/adf.c, seeded with its
   committed corpus and one seed of ten of the new commands (build/fuzz/corpus/driver/i-seed1):

       build/fuzz/driver build/fuzz/corpus/driver -max_total_time=60 -rss_limit_mb=2048

   Result: "Done 27666 runs in 61 second(s)", 453 executions per second, peak RSS 686 MB, no crash.

What these runs assert: fuzz_text_idele.c asserts the contract listed in its header comment (statuses, agreement of
classify and the parsers, the output untouched on a status, the predicate of the value, the printed text well formed
and of the same kind, the re-reading of the printed text encloses); fuzz_driver.c asserts what its header says.
What they do not do: run for an hour or more, compare with the Python reference (the comparison with the reference
is the vector test tests/test_text_idele.c: 2200 texts, and 1500 balls for the printer), or run alone at night.
